class:
    patterns:
        [a|] cad vertex
    members:
        point as a cad vector3
        provenance as a cad provenance
class:
    patterns:
        [a|] cad edge
    members:
        curve as a cad curve key
        startParameter as a 64 bit floating-point number
        endParameter as a 64 bit floating-point number
        start as a cad vertex key
        end as a cad vertex key
        coedges as the type of (a cad topology list of a cad coedge key)
        provenance as a cad provenance
class:
    patterns:
        [a|] cad coedge
    members:
        edge as a cad edge key
        forward as a boolean
        pcurve as a cad pcurve result
        owner as a cad loop key
        provenance as a cad provenance
class:
    patterns:
        [a|] cad loop
    members:
        coedges as the type of (a cad topology list of a cad coedge key)
        owner as a cad face key
        provenance as a cad provenance
class:
    patterns:
        [a|] cad face
    members:
        surface as a cad surface key
        forward as a boolean
        loops as the type of (a cad topology list of a cad loop key)
        owner as a cad shell key
        provenance as a cad provenance
class:
    patterns:
        [a|] cad shell
    members:
        faces as the type of (a cad topology list of a cad face key)
        owner as a cad lump key
        provenance as a cad provenance
class:
    patterns:
        [a|] cad lump
    members:
        shells as the type of (a cad topology list of a cad shell key)
        provenance as a cad provenance

to get a cad vertex at {cad vector3:point} with provenance {cad provenance:provenance}:
    return @intrinsic("construct", a cad vertex, point, provenance)
to get a cad edge on {cad curve key:curve} from {a number:first} to {a number:last} between {cad vertex key:start} and {cad vertex key:end} with provenance {cad provenance:provenance}:
    return @intrinsic("construct", a cad edge, curve, first as a 64 bit floating-point number, last as a 64 bit floating-point number, start, end, a cad topology list of a cad coedge key, provenance)
to get a cad coedge on {cad edge key:edge} forward {boolean:forward} with pcurve {cad pcurve result:pcurve} owned by {cad loop key:owner} with provenance {cad provenance:provenance}:
    return @intrinsic("construct", a cad coedge, edge, forward, pcurve, owner, provenance)
to get a cad loop owned by {cad face key:owner} with provenance {cad provenance:provenance}:
    return @intrinsic("construct", a cad loop, a cad topology list of a cad coedge key, owner, provenance)
to get a cad face on {cad surface key:surface} forward {boolean:forward} owned by {cad shell key:owner} with provenance {cad provenance:provenance}:
    return @intrinsic("construct", a cad face, surface, forward, a cad topology list of a cad loop key, owner, provenance)
to get a cad shell owned by {cad lump key:owner} with provenance {cad provenance:provenance}:
    return @intrinsic("construct", a cad shell, a cad topology list of a cad face key, owner, provenance)
to get a cad lump with provenance {cad provenance:provenance}:
    return @intrinsic("construct", a cad lump, a cad topology list of a cad shell key, provenance)

to get the cad payload clone of {cad vertex:original}:
    return original
to get the cad payload clone of {cad edge:original}:
    set result to original
    set result's coedges to the cad clone of original's coedges
    return result
to get the cad payload clone of {cad coedge:original}:
    set result to original
    set result's pcurve to the cad clone of original's pcurve
    return result

to get the cad payload clone of {cad loop:original}:
    set result to original
    set result's coedges to the cad clone of original's coedges
    return result

to get the cad payload clone of {cad face:original}:
    set result to original
    set result's loops to the cad clone of original's loops
    return result

to get the cad payload clone of {cad shell:original}:
    set result to original
    set result's faces to the cad clone of original's faces
    return result

to get the cad payload clone of {cad lump:original}:
    set result to original
    set result's shells to the cad clone of original's shells
    return result

to get the cad payload clone of {cad surface:original}:
    return the cad clone of original

to get the cad payload clone of {cad edge curve3:original}:
    return the cad clone of original

# Source-derived node equality compares every field in declaration order.
to get {cad vertex:first} = {cad vertex:second}:
    if (((first's point's x = second's point's x) and (first's point's y = second's point's y)) and (first's point's z = second's point's z)) = false:
        return false
    if (first's provenance = second's provenance) = false:
        return false
    return true
to get the cad clone of {cad vertex:original}:
    return the cad payload clone of original

to get {cad edge:first} = {cad edge:second}:
    if (first's curve = second's curve) = false:
        return false
    if (first's startParameter = second's startParameter) = false:
        return false
    if (first's endParameter = second's endParameter) = false:
        return false
    if (first's start = second's start) = false:
        return false
    if (first's end = second's end) = false:
        return false
    if (cad topology lists first's coedges and second's coedges are equal) = false:
        return false
    if (first's provenance = second's provenance) = false:
        return false
    return true
to get the cad clone of {cad edge:original}:
    return the cad payload clone of original

to get {cad coedge:first} = {cad coedge:second}:
    if (first's edge = second's edge) = false:
        return false
    if (first's forward = second's forward) = false:
        return false
    if (first's pcurve = second's pcurve) = false:
        return false
    if (first's owner = second's owner) = false:
        return false
    if (first's provenance = second's provenance) = false:
        return false
    return true
to get the cad clone of {cad coedge:original}:
    return the cad payload clone of original

to get {cad loop:first} = {cad loop:second}:
    if (cad topology lists first's coedges and second's coedges are equal) = false:
        return false
    if (first's owner = second's owner) = false:
        return false
    if (first's provenance = second's provenance) = false:
        return false
    return true
to get the cad clone of {cad loop:original}:
    return the cad payload clone of original

to get {cad face:first} = {cad face:second}:
    if (first's surface = second's surface) = false:
        return false
    if (first's forward = second's forward) = false:
        return false
    if (cad topology lists first's loops and second's loops are equal) = false:
        return false
    if (first's owner = second's owner) = false:
        return false
    if (first's provenance = second's provenance) = false:
        return false
    return true
to get the cad clone of {cad face:original}:
    return the cad payload clone of original

to get {cad shell:first} = {cad shell:second}:
    if (cad topology lists first's faces and second's faces are equal) = false:
        return false
    if (first's owner = second's owner) = false:
        return false
    if (first's provenance = second's provenance) = false:
        return false
    return true
to get the cad clone of {cad shell:original}:
    return the cad payload clone of original

to get {cad lump:first} = {cad lump:second}:
    if (cad topology lists first's shells and second's shells are equal) = false:
        return false
    if (first's provenance = second's provenance) = false:
        return false
    return true
to get the cad clone of {cad lump:original}:
    return the cad payload clone of original

# Body storage owns all nine arenas and the ordered root list.
class:
    patterns:
        [a|] cad body storage
    members:
        vertices
        edges
        coedges
        loops
        faces
        shells
        lumps
        surfaces
        curves
        roots
        references as a pointer to an integer
    retain:
        set owner to the references of @intrinsic("lifecycle value")
        if owner != (0 as a pointer to an integer):
            set count to @intrinsic("dereference", owner)
            if count = 2147483647:
                abort the program
            @intrinsic("store at", owner, count + 1)
    release:
        set owner to the references of @intrinsic("lifecycle value")
        if owner != (0 as a pointer to an integer):
            set count to @intrinsic("dereference", owner)
            if count = 1:
                free cad arena (the vertices of @intrinsic("lifecycle value"))
                free cad arena (the edges of @intrinsic("lifecycle value"))
                free cad arena (the coedges of @intrinsic("lifecycle value"))
                free cad arena (the loops of @intrinsic("lifecycle value"))
                free cad arena (the faces of @intrinsic("lifecycle value"))
                free cad arena (the shells of @intrinsic("lifecycle value"))
                free cad arena (the lumps of @intrinsic("lifecycle value"))
                free cad arena (the surfaces of @intrinsic("lifecycle value"))
                free cad arena (the curves of @intrinsic("lifecycle value"))
                free (the roots of @intrinsic("lifecycle value"))
                @intrinsic("call", "libc", "free", nothing, owner)
            else:
                @intrinsic("store at", owner, count - 1)

class:
    patterns:
        [a|] cad body
    members:
        vertices
        edges
        coedges
        loops
        faces
        shells
        lumps
        surfaces
        curves
        roots
        provenance as a cad provenance
        storage as a cad body storage

local function the cad body using {cad body storage:storage} with provenance {cad provenance:provenance}:
    execute:
        return @intrinsic("construct", a cad body, storage's vertices, storage's edges, storage's coedges, storage's loops, storage's faces, storage's shells, storage's lumps, storage's surfaces, storage's curves, storage's roots, provenance, storage)
to get an empty cad body:
    set vertices to a cad arena of a cad vertex
    set edges to a cad arena of a cad edge
    set coedges to a cad arena of a cad coedge
    set loops to a cad arena of a cad loop
    set faces to a cad arena of a cad face
    set shells to a cad arena of a cad shell
    set lumps to a cad arena of a cad lump
    set surfaces to a cad arena of the type of (the cad surface of the cad xy plane)
    set curves to a cad arena of the type of (the cad edge curve3 of (a cad line3 with origin the cad zero vector3 and direction the cad x axis))
    set roots to an empty list of a cad lump key
    set storage to @intrinsic("construct", a cad body storage, vertices, edges, coedges, loops, faces, shells, lumps, surfaces, curves, roots, a cad topology reference counter)
    return the cad body using storage with provenance the synthesized cad provenance
to get the cad default body:
    return an empty cad body
to get the cad clone of {cad body:original}:
    set vertices to the cad clone of original's vertices
    set edges to the cad clone of original's edges
    set coedges to the cad clone of original's coedges
    set loops to the cad clone of original's loops
    set faces to the cad clone of original's faces
    set shells to the cad clone of original's shells
    set lumps to the cad clone of original's lumps
    set surfaces to the cad clone of original's surfaces
    set curves to the cad clone of original's curves
    set roots to an empty list of a cad lump key
    loop index from 0 to the length of original's roots:
        append (the item at index in original's roots) to roots
    set storage to @intrinsic("construct", a cad body storage, vertices, edges, coedges, loops, faces, shells, lumps, surfaces, curves, roots, a cad topology reference counter)
    return the cad body using storage with provenance original's provenance

to get the cad body key after inserting {cad vertex:value} into {cad body:body}:
    return the cad vertex key from (the cad key after inserting value into body's vertices)
to get the cad node pointer for {cad vertex key:key} in {cad body:body}:
    return the cad node pointer for (the cad arena key of key) in body's vertices
to get the cad lookup of {cad vertex key:key} in {cad body:body}:
    return the cad lookup of (the cad arena key of key) in body's vertices
to get the cad removal of {cad vertex key:key} from {cad body:body}:
    return the cad removal of (the cad arena key of key) from body's vertices
to replace cad node {cad vertex key:key} in {cad body:body} with {cad vertex:value}:
